cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: >
  If you use this software, please cite the repository and the PICLas paper given under "references".
  This project has been developed with the help of many contributors.
  A list of contributors can be found in "CONTRIBUTORS.md".
  piclas-db does not contain or redistribute any data. If you use a database built with piclas-db,
  please also cite the original data sources (e.g. the LXCat databases, NIST or ATcT) as stated in
  the references stored in the database.

title: "piclas-db: Build, check and convert PICLas species and cross-section databases from original sources such as LXCat and NIST"
abstract: >
  piclas-db is a command-line tool that builds the species and cross-section databases read by PICLas
  (database.h5, layout of SpeciesDatabase.h5) locally from the original data sources. It guides the user
  through the download, stores the original files in a local store, converts between the original formats,
  ASCII tables and HDF5, checks existing (also legacy) database files for inconsistencies, and supports the
  validation of the data with PICLas reservoir simulations.
